From 3d8bd7de656835e3d94feed8fe1423cd2c3d4f06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:34:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 075/274] DeepSeek V4.1 prefill SP: unreduced results that
 TileLang mHC adds in rank order

The rank-order reduce-scatter's exchange can receive into a caller's buffer
(exchange_into, which also takes row ranges of larger buffers), and
RankOrderParts carries every rank's partial of this rank's rows in one
(world, L, ...) tensor. TileLang mHC's post_pre takes those parts and adds them
in FP32 in rank order as it loads them, rounding once, so its outputs have the
bits of the summed input; post and the SP gather sum them first.

SPRows gains an unreduced mode: project_reduce_scatter then projects each
block into a send buffer (this rank's own straight into its slot of the parts)
and exchanges, in slices on the side stream as before, without the sum or the
copy back. The MoE runner takes a model-installed reduce-scatter hook that
writes the shared + routed sum per row block and returns the parts, and the
decoder layer wraps both SP results. sp_prefill.UNREDUCED is off, so nothing
changes yet.

(cherry picked from commit cdebef6f0b37822287c42e1c5c7b3039727baa7c)

